# INTRODUCED: Stage 3 — Security Gates
# PURPOSE: Placeholder showing where your Cosign public key belongs.
#
# SETUP:
#   1. Generate your keypair on your host machine (Stage 3, Step 1):
#        cosign generate-key-pair
#      This creates cosign.key (NEVER commit this) and cosign.pub
#
#   2. Replace this file with your actual cosign.pub:
#        cp cosign.pub infra/cosign.pub
#
#   3. Paste the key content into infra/policies/require-signed-images.yaml
#      in the publicKeys field
#
#   4. Commit infra/cosign.pub to the infra repo — it is a public key,
#      safe to commit. The private key (cosign.key) must NEVER be committed.
#
# The cosign.key is added to GitHub Secrets as COSIGN_PRIVATE_KEY.
# The cosign.pub lives here in Git so Kyverno can verify signatures.
#
# Example public key format (yours will look like this):
-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
MFkwEwYHKoZIzj0CAQYIKoZIzj0DAQcDQgAE<YOUR_KEY_CONTENT_HERE>
-----END PUBLIC KEY-----
